<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<lint>
    <!--
        TV manifest checks, ignored ONLY for the firetv flavor overlay.

        Lint evaluates a flavor manifest in ISOLATION, not as merged. The firetv
        overlay contains nothing but two `tools:node="remove"` permission
        entries — no activity, no uses-feature, no uses-sdk — so every check
        that asks "is this a well-formed TV manifest?" answers no and anchors
        its report to the <manifest> element there.

        The firetvRelease MERGED manifest is correct, verified from the merge
        output:

            uses-sdk        minSdk=24  targetSdk=36
            uses-feature    android.software.leanback     required=false
            uses-feature    android.hardware.touchscreen  required=false
            activity        tv.onscreen.android.ui.MainActivity
                            categories: LEANBACK_LAUNCHER, DEFAULT, BROWSABLE

        Scoped by PATH rather than disabled module-wide, so a genuine instance
        of any of these in src/main (where the real manifest lives) still fails
        the build. This is the whole reason the ignores are here and not in a
        `lint { disable += ... }` block.

        Why a list rather than fixing them one at a time: they are three
        symptoms of one cause. Suppressing them individually as they surfaced
        just produced the next one in the queue — MissingLeanbackLauncher, then
        ImpliedTouchscreenHardware, then MissingLeanbackSupport. Any future TV
        manifest check will do the same against this file.
    -->
    <issue id="MissingLeanbackLauncher">
        <ignore path="src/firetv/AndroidManifest.xml" />
    </issue>
    <issue id="MissingLeanbackSupport">
        <ignore path="src/firetv/AndroidManifest.xml" />
    </issue>
    <issue id="ImpliedTouchscreenHardware">
        <ignore path="src/firetv/AndroidManifest.xml" />
    </issue>
</lint>
